<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How personal data is handled on the Orthodent Specialized Dental Clinic website."
  actualizado="1 January 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Orthodent Specialized Dental Clinic</strong>, based at Uniplaza La Ceiba, Cortés,
    Honduras, is the controller of the personal data collected through this website.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Personal data we collect</h2>
  <p>We may collect the following information when you provide it voluntarily:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Full name.</li>
    <li>Phone or WhatsApp number.</li>
    <li>Reason for consultation or specialty of interest.</li>
    <li>Browsing data (IP address, browser, pages visited) through cookies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Purpose of processing</h2>
  <p>We use your data to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Respond to and manage appointment requests sent via the form or WhatsApp.</li>
    <li>Confirm availability, provide general clinical information and coordinate care.</li>
    <li>Improve the user experience and analyse site usage, where applicable.</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations or requirements from competent authorities.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    Processing is based on your consent, given when you submit your request, and on the legitimate
    interest of Orthodent in managing the care you request, always respecting your rights.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep the information necessary to attend to your request for as long as is reasonably
    required to follow it up, and for the period mandated by applicable law. Browsing data is
    retained for the duration of the cookies you accept.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Sharing with third parties</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent or share your personal data with third parties for commercial purposes. We
    may share it only when necessary to comply with legal obligations, or with service providers
    (hosting, maps or analytics) under confidentiality clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some services (maps, social media or infrastructure) may process data outside Honduras. In such
    cases we adopt reasonable measures to ensure an adequate level of protection, as required by
    applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You may exercise the following rights at any time:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access to your personal data.</li>
    <li>Rectification of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
    <li>Deletion of your data (where applicable).</li>
    <li>Restriction of or objection to processing.</li>
    <li>Withdrawal of consent, without affecting the lawfulness of prior processing.</li>
    <li>Filing a complaint with the competent data protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise these rights, contact us at:
    <a href="mailto:dra.karenchinchilla@gmail.com">dra.karenchinchilla@gmail.com</a>. We will respond within a
    reasonable period.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Cookies and consent</h2>
  <p>
    We use a cookie banner to request your consent before loading optional cookies (for example, to
    display the clinic map). You may accept, reject or change your preference at any time. See the
    relevant section in our cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We apply reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data against loss,
    unauthorised access, alteration or destruction. However, no internet transmission system is
    completely secure.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this privacy policy when necessary to reflect changes in our practices or in
    applicable law. The current version is the one published on this website, with the update date
    shown above.
  </p>
</Legal>